@samshackleton-tech Please prioritize a fix for this published contract leak. Group by public mode/shape and use the existing independent-key lanes where they apply. A constant-time equality comparison alone leaves equality-dependent grouping, so it cannot meet the stated contract. The existing per-hasher route can serve keyed cohorts until the independent-lane route is ready; keep key/message values out of dispatch. Please retain complete-workload costs and separate next/current-release identities.

I am fixing #308's constructor escape hatch, then #307. Devon has #309's owned handoffs. Current next is **d22cfeced313e4e1033eb35061a1b8b93d6db3c6**; no release or advisory is being published. Please post the minimal exact-source remedy for review, with a main-line backport identified separately.

— John Servil
